Requirements: 29   with obligations: 28   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Obligation derivation reads one requirement at a time and produces obligations
    for it alone, so a requirement stated in two places yields two obligations that
    assert the same thing. On one observed task file, 34 requirements produced 71
    obligations. Every later stage runs once per obligation, so the duplication
    multiplies the work and the length of the report while adding nothing.
    -> obligation-derive-per-requirement-then-link-duplicates  [functional/explicit]
       Run obligation derivation one requirement at a time so that a requirement stated
       in multiple places can produce duplicate obligations that are later linked.
    -> obligation-duplicate-obligations-for-repeated-requirements  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that a requirement stated in two places yields two
       obligations that assert the same thing before any later linking pass runs.
    -> obligation-duplication-multiplies-work-and-report-length  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that duplicated obligations increase later-stage work and
       report length without adding new information.

[task-02] The duplication is not a fault in the input. A mandate and its acceptance
    criteria naturally restate each other, and a requirement is often followed by a
    clause giving the reason for it. Both are ordinary ways to write a requirement, and
    both currently produce a second obligation.
    -> obligation-treat-restated-requirements-as-ordinary-input  [functional/explicit]
       Treat a mandate and its acceptance criteria, and a requirement followed by its
       reason clause, as ordinary requirement restatements that currently produce a
       second obligation.
    -> obligation-reason-clause-is-ordinary-requirement-form  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that a requirement followed by a clause giving its reason
       is treated as an ordinary way to write that requirement.
    -> obligation-acceptance-criteria-restates-mandate  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that a mandate and its acceptance criteria are treated as
       restatements of the same requirement.

[task-03] Add a pass that runs after derivation and recognises when two obligations
    state the same requirement. Its output is a link rather than a deletion: the
    surviving obligation is named by every requirement that stated it.
    -> obligation-add-post-derivation-duplicate-linking-pass  [functional/explicit]
       Add a pass after derivation that recognises when two obligations state the same
       requirement and links the surviving obligation to every requirement that stated
       it.
    -> obligation-link-instead-of-delete  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that duplicate recognition produces a link rather than
       deleting an obligation or discarding requirement text.

[constraint-01] The pass runs after obligation derivation, over the obligations
    derivation produced, rather than inside derivation.
    -> post-derivation-linking-pass  [functional/explicit]
       Run the duplicate-recognition pass after obligation derivation, operating on the
       produced obligations rather than inside derivation.

[constraint-02] Recognising a duplicate produces a link from a second requirement to an
    existing obligation. No obligation is deleted and no requirement text is discarded.
    -> duplicate-recognition-links-existing-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       Represent a recognized duplicate as a link from the later requirement to an
       existing obligation while preserving both the obligation and the requirement
       text.

[constraint-03] A linked obligation carries the union of the requirement links and the
    union of the source spans of everything merged into it, so it still traces to every
    piece of task text that produced it.
    -> linked-obligation-merges-provenance  [invariant/explicit]
       Carry forward the union of requirement links and the union of source spans from
       everything merged into a linked obligation.

[constraint-04] The links are typed fields in the schema-constrained response. A link
    stated in an obligation's description, rationale, or any other free-text field does
    not count as a link.
    -> typed-link-fields-only  [compatibility/explicit]
       Express links as typed schema fields, with link meaning not inferred from free-
       text fields.

[constraint-05] Two obligations about the same area of the change are not necessarily
    the same requirement. Where the judgement is uncertain, leave them separate.
    -> uncertain-duplicates-remain-separate  [human_review/explicit]
       Keep obligations separate when the judgment about whether they are the same
       requirement is uncertain.

[constraint-06] A requirement and a clause giving the reason for that requirement state
    one requirement, not two.
    -> reason-clause-counts-as-same-requirement  [functional/explicit]
       Treat a requirement and its reason clause as one requirement rather than two.

[constraint-07] The obligations derivation produced, before any linking, are persisted
    in the review state. They are provenance rather than report content.
    -> persist-prelink-derivation-in-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       Persist the obligations derivation produced before linking in the review state as
       provenance rather than report content.

[constraint-08] Editing one requirement leaves the obligations derived for the other
    requirements unchanged.
    -> editing-one-requirement-preserves-others-derived-obligations  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the derived obligations for unaffected requirements when one requirement
       is edited.

[constraint-09] The links this pass produces are identical unless the derived
    obligations they were computed from change.
    -> links-stable-unless-derived-obligations-change  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep the links produced by the pass stable whenever the derived obligations they
       were computed from remain unchanged.

[constraint-10] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state, both for the derived obligations and for the linked result.
    -> byte-identical-task-text-produces-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]
       Make two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state
       for both the derived obligations and the linked result.

[constraint-11] Typed schemas are pydantic models, as the rest of the repository defines
    them.
    -> typed-schemas-use-pydantic-models  [compatibility/explicit]
       Represent the typed schemas as pydantic models, matching the repository's
       existing schema style.

[constraint-12] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-avoid-live-model-calls  [error_handling/explicit]
       Keep tests free of live model calls.

[exclusion-01] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> scope-exclusion-obligation-splitting-granularity-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the existing scope around how finely a single requirement is split into
       obligations.

[exclusion-02] Measuring how accurate the links are, which is #211.
    -> scope-exclusion-link-accuracy-measurement-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the existing scope around measuring how accurate the links are.

[exclusion-03] The wording of the decomposition prompt beyond what this pass requires,
    which is #205, #206 and #219.
    -> scope-exclusion-prompt-wording-beyond-required-pass-unchanged  [docs_config/explicit]
       Preserve the existing scope around wording of the decomposition prompt beyond
       what this pass requires.

[exclusion-04] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> obligation-evidence-not-required  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that an obligation does not need test evidence to be
       considered valid.

[exclusion-05] Recovering requirements that an earlier run dropped.
    -> obligation-no-recovery-of-dropped-requirements  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the behavior that earlier dropped requirements are not recovered by this
       change.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       This is a section marker naming the implementation area, with no checkable
       requirement content by itself.

[completion-02] A task file stating one requirement in two sections yields one
    obligation linked to both requirements, whose source spans cover both statements.
    -> one-obligation-for-two-sections  [functional/explicit]
       A task file that states one requirement in two sections produces one linked
       obligation whose provenance includes both requirement statements.

[completion-03] A test asserts that two distinct requirements sharing vocabulary are not
    linked to one obligation.
    -> separate-distinct-requirements  [invariant/explicit]
       Distinct requirements that merely share vocabulary remain separate and are not
       linked to one obligation.

[completion-04] A test asserts that a requirement followed by a clause giving its reason
    yields one obligation rather than two.
    -> reason-clause-single-requirement  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement followed by a clause giving its reason is treated as one
       requirement and produces one obligation.

[completion-05] A test asserts that the obligations derivation produced, before linking,
    are present in the persisted review state.
    -> persist-pre-link-derivation  [invariant/explicit]
       The obligations derivation produced before linking is present in the persisted
       review state.

[completion-06] A test asserts that a link is expressed as a typed field, and that the
    response schema cannot express a link as free text.
    -> typed-link-field-only  [compatibility/explicit]
       A link is represented as a typed schema field, and the response schema cannot
       represent that link as free text.

[completion-07] A test asserts that two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-
    identical review state at both the derived and the linked stage.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state at
       both the derived and linked stages.

[completion-08] A test asserts that editing one requirement leaves the obligations
    derived for the other requirements unchanged.
    -> editing-one-leaves-others-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       Editing one requirement leaves the obligations derived for the other requirements
       unchanged.

[completion-09] A test asserts that the links are unchanged when the derived obligations
    they were computed from are unchanged.
    -> links-stable-when-derived-obligations-unchanged  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve link outputs when the derived obligations they were computed from are
       unchanged.

